       <p class="prose">Every calculator tells you it's an estimate, shown right next to your score, not buried in fine print. We use publicly released College Board scoring worksheets and recent score distributions to project cut-offs, and update them each cycle.</p>
       <p class="prose">No ads, no sign-ups, no gated features. Just the tool. <a href="/about/">How the estimates are built &rsaquo;</a></p>
     </section>
+    <section class="sec" id="use-in-ai"><h2 class="h2">Use this data in Claude or ChatGPT</h2>
+      <p class="prose">The AP score distributions on this site are also available as a free MCP server. An AI assistant can use it to look up the College Board score distribution for an AP exam, find the percentile of a score, rank exams by pass rate, and estimate a score from a composite on the seven exams with a printed worksheet. The data covers 2024, 2025 and 2026. There is no account or API key.</p>
+      <p class="prose"><strong>Claude.ai or ChatGPT.</strong> Add a custom connector with this URL.</p>
+      <pre style="margin:0 0 10px;padding:11px 13px;background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--s200);border-radius:var(--radius);font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12.5px;overflow-x:auto;white-space:pre;color:var(--ink);"><code>https://ap-score-distributions-mcp.lipmichal.workers.dev/mcp</code></pre>
+      <p class="prose"><strong>Claude Code.</strong></p>
+      <pre style="margin:0 0 10px;padding:11px 13px;background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--s200);border-radius:var(--radius);font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12.5px;overflow-x:auto;white-space:pre;color:var(--ink);"><code>claude mcp add --transport http ap-score-distributions https://ap-score-distributions-mcp.lipmichal.workers.dev/mcp</code></pre>
+      <p class="prose"><a href="https://www.mcpstamp.com/free-servers/ap-score-distributions-mcp/">Setup steps &rsaquo;</a> &middot; <a href="https://github.com/theluckystrike/ap-score-distributions-mcp">Source on GitHub &rsaquo;</a></p>
+    </section>
